  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have a **simple weighted complete undirected** graph on a vertex set with NNN vertices, numbered 111 to NNN. The weights follow a special property as described below.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of size NNN (1≤Ai≤201 \\le A_i \\le 201≤Ai​≤20), and the weight of the edge joining vertices XXX and YYY can be described as follows:\n\n\nIf AX=AYA_X = A_YAX​=AY​, the weight is ∣X−Y∣|X - Y|∣X−Y∣\nIf AX≠AYA_X \\ne A_YAX​=AY​, the weight is 2⋅∣X−Y∣2 \\cdot |X - Y|2⋅∣X−Y∣\nYou are given QQQ queries, each containing 222 nodes XXX and YYY, and you must print the distance between vertex XXX and vertex YYY. The distance is defined as the smallest sum of weights on a path from XXX to YYY.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains 222 integers each - NNN and QQQ, the number of vertices and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe next QQQ lines contain 222 integers each - XXX and YYY, representing a query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output QQQ integers on a single line, the answers to the queries in order.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤4⋅1042 \\le N \\le 4 \\cdot 10^42≤N≤4⋅104",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1061 \\le Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^61≤Q≤2⋅106",
      "1≤Ai≤201 \\le A_i \\le 201≤Ai​≤20",
      "1≤X,Y≤N1 \\le X, Y \\le N1≤X,Y≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 4⋅1044 \\cdot 10^44⋅104",
      "The sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1062 \\cdot 10^62⋅106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
